WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.360
So, what is it?

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.810
It's about Yui-chan.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.150
F-Furukawa?

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:14.330
You see, I talked to Yui-chan while
we were waiting for you all today.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:14.960
Okay.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.460
And I think we got to be pretty close.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.700
I see. That's great.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:26.390
At times, I have these moments where I think I might be bad with people.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.590
I want to be friendly with everyone I meet,

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.450
but there are times when I just don't know what to talk about.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.260
But, you know, I want to talk with Yui-chan much, much more.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:39.640
I see.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.500
It's probably because I think of Yui-chan like a little sister.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.600
A little sister?

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.150
Speaking of which, Yui-chan said that you were like a father.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:50.190
A father?!

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.340
Yui-chan's kind of different, isn't she?

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.130
A father, huh...

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.060
Do I look that old?

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:01.540
Sou-kun, when you think of Yui-chan...

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:03.040
Huh? What?

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.040
No, nothing. Night.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.320
Sure.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.790
This is our first time together, isn't it?

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:50.440
Yes.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:54.140
I've always wished that I could have a little sister.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.980
We'd be able to wash each other in the bath

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:01.320
and tell each other things
that we couldn't tell anyone else.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.480
Things you could not tell anyone else?

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.150
Yes.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.410
Is there any chance you feel like sharing yet?

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:14.170
There just might be something
I can do to help, too.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.170
If I could, I would like to...

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:21.470
No, there was even a time when I did.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.180
My old self...

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.360
Hey, Akiyama.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.350
Have you decided on a career path yet?

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:36.020
Oh... Right, well...

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:39.600
The look on your face says
you haven't given it any thought.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.290
Make sure you do.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:45.630
If you're not careful, never mind your career—
you could even end up jeopardizing your graduation.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:46.920
Yes, sir.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:50.280
It just came out of nowhere, you know?

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.330
I got asked about my career path too.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:56.230
You'll all be pulled in for a meeting once the school festival is over.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.550
It happens every year.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:59.690
Oh, I had no idea.

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.920
Anyway, what about you, Airi?

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.010
You're going to college, right?

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:06.620
Me? Of course, I plan to go on to college, but...

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:07.890
Oh, thank you.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.410
To be honest, I still can't decide on a major.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.980
Going into law and becoming an attorney or something would be cool,

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:17.440
but going into the sciences and becoming a researcher sounds interesting too.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.570
You're solid at both the sciences and humanities, after all.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.280
Huh...

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.280
What about you, Kaori?
What's your career plan?

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:26.040
Me?

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.540
Hm, well...

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.310
I plan to go somewhere with a
domestic sciences department.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:32.320
Huh...

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.320
I want to become a certified nutritionist.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.330
That's great!

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.060
You'll be an even more unattainable flower.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.470
You're not making any sense, Kenny-kun.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.800
You guys have planned further ahead than I thought.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:50.330
Eh, I wasn't planning to think about it
until I got back stateside.

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:52.970
I might just get told
to go work right away anyway.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:55.560
Oh, right, you're going back.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.780
What about you, Sou-kun?

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:58.610
Aren't you going for astronomy or something like that?

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.840
That's right.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:03.370
Somewhere you can study space engineering or whatever.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:04.860
Space engineering, huh?

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.860
Sou-san will be fine.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:09.330
When the time comes, he'll be able
to choose properly for himself.

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.410
D-Do you think so?

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.630
For example, even with love,

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:16.940
when the time comes,
you have to choose one person.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:18.380
It's the same thing, Sou.

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:20.590
Jennifer again?

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.970
Let's see. What do you have this time?

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:27.100
What the heck is this?

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:31.160
A photo of her winning an eating contest!

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:37.340
Oh, that reminds me, the pictures we took at the river should be ready today.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:38.650
I'll go pick them up.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.600
I also have something to take care of,
so you'll have to excuse me.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.430
But before I do, Airi-san,
I believe you have something for Yui-san.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:45.370
Right.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:46.100
Here.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:47.360
What is this?

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.990
A badge that says you're a member of the Astronomy Club.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.700
This is coming a little late, but...

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.160
We all have one.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:58.420
With this, you're an official member of our team.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:00.760
We've got the school festival, of course,

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:05.000
but it's our way of saying that we hope you'll
continue to feel welcome among us after that, too.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:07.430
Uh, um...

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.810
Thank you very much.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.170
Nagisa-senpai, is something wrong?

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:31.030
What do you think of Yui-san?

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:34.110
Uh, well...

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:37.500
Nothing especially.
I think she's a normal, nice girl.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.770
You're right. She is a nice girl.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:43.710
Um, but that doesn't mean I have
...special feelings for her or anything...

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:44.680
What?

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:46.380
Mm-hm.

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:49.340
M-More importantly,
what did you need to take care of?

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:54.970
It's fine. Let's just go get
the photos together.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.810
What? Uh, okay...

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:04.990
These turned out quite well.

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:06.600
This one, for instance. Take a look.

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:09.360
Oh, that <i>is</i> good. I'm glad.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:12.570
Yui-san looks great in this photo, too.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:15.670
I had no idea Airi'd even snapped this.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:20.040
Hey, since we have these,
why don't we put them up in the club room?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.260
Yeah, all right.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:23.400
Shall we put them up on the bulletin board?

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.320
We can order extra prints
...of the ones we want and—

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.760
Oh, go ahead. You can get that.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:37.830
Nagisa-senpai?

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.280
They hung up.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:42.770
Yeah, I guess...

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:45.130
You're not going to call them back?

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.560
It's fine. It's probably nothing impor—

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.500
You wanted to see me, Father?

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.120
Yes. Well, have a seat.

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:03.710
About that matchmaking meeting the other day...

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:07.460
It seems Hikaru-kun took
quite a liking to you as well.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:11.340
As long as you're in agreement,
we're talking of exchanging betrothal gifts.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.740
Father, I am planning to go to college and—

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:15.150
I know that.

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:17.180
I won't object to your going to college.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:22.180
But you do understand that
this match is not just about you?

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:24.190
Yes.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:28.040
This has to do with our group
and the Reito Group.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:31.610
Both of our trading companies,
affiliate companies, and subcontractors...

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.200
All of their futures are riding on this.

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.960
Yes, I am well aware.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:39.500
Good. As long as you understand,
we're done here.

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:42.460
Yes, sir. Please excuse me.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.240
Nagisa, tomorrow is Saturday, isn't it?

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:50.460
Yes. I have classes in the morning, though...

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:53.970
It just so happens that we're holding a meeting regarding merging operations,

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:57.340
and Hikaru-kun is supposed to be coming by the house.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:00.330
You should get back home
as soon as you can, too.

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:02.360
Spend some time together.

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:03.620
I understand.

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:08.230
Senpai...

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.680
Are you sure it's okay?

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:13.940
It's okay.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:16.730
Never mind that, let me hear about you.

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:17.870
Me?

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.360
You're not so enthusiastic
about space engineering?

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:21.410
Oh...

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:24.250
Environmental sciences, physical chemistry...

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:28.240
There are actually a lot of choices
when it comes to studying astronomy.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:29.940
If you'd like, I could loan you a book.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:32.090
Nagisa-senpai...

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:36.330
It's not that I'm not sure or anything.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:38.650
I just don't want to think about it.

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:39.420
What?

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:42.680
It's not that I don't care about the future,

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:47.230
but I'm mystified as to why I should have to be
in a rush to narrow things down right this minute.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:50.170
It's not that I'm trying to escape from it,

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:52.060
but I want a little more of what
I have now, taking it easy—

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:55.060
or rather, enjoying the time I have. That's kind of how I feel.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.840
I guess that's a bad philosophy to have, huh?

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:04.190
Sou-san, I sometimes feel that way too.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:07.080
Wishing that things could stay the way they are now forever.

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:10.360
In the past, I'd never desired anything.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:13.340
There was nothing I wanted
and nothing I didn't want to lose.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.840
There was no future I wished to seek.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:21.040
But the current members of the
Astronomy Club are very dear to me.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:23.610
It's the first thing that
I've ever wanted to not lose.

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:25.720
Senpai...

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:27.270
I'm in love.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:28.020
Huh?!

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:29.850
I'm in love, you see.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.020
Huh? Wh-What?

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:34.880
With having lunch with everyone in the Astronomy Club,

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.680
talking about inconsequential things,

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:39.740
and being dragged into ridiculous conflicts.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:42.990
R-Right! It's fun, isn't it?

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.490
Sou-san, what has you so flustered?

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:50.300
Don't look at me like that.

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:55.410
Okay, then. I'm going back to school.

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:57.050
I'll come too.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:59.470
Oh? I thought you had
something to take care of.

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:04.430
Nagisa-san.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:04.970
Oh...

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:13.200
I was on my way home from your place, where I'd hoped to see you again, but...

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:14.020
I'm glad.

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:16.390
Um, who is this?

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.400
Reito Hikaru-san.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:22.820
Heir to the Reito Group, and my fiancé.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.040
I see...

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:25.910
F-Fiancé?!

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:28.160
Nice to meet you. I'm Reito.

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:30.840
What? U-Uh, um...

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.630
N-Nice to meet you.

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:34.080
And this is?

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.540
Akiyama Sou-san.

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:37.620
He and I are going out.

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:40.920
H-Hello. I-I'm Akiyama.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:43.840
Wait...

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:47.240
You're quite the heartbreaker, Nagisa-san.

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:49.740
I'd thought to take you for a drive or something today, but...

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:51.580
Let us go for this drive.

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:55.220
Now. The three of us.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:02.110
How did I end up in this mess?

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:04.820
<i>This person is Nagisa-senpai's fiancé</i>

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:07.790
<i>and he's taking her out on a drive for a date...</i>

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.460
<i>So what am I doing here?</i>

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:12.860
Akiyama-kun, was it?

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:14.250
Huh? Oh, yes.

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:17.460
What's Nagisa-san like at school?

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:20.040
What? Nagisa-senpai?

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:24.800
She's beautiful, and smart,
..and good at everything, and...

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:29.860
It's kind of like, she teases ordinary mortals like me to amuse herself, I guess.

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:33.290
That doesn't exactly tell me much.

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:36.020
What kind of person is Akiyama-kun from your perspective, Nagisa-san?

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:38.680
Sou-san is absentminded,

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:41.050
marches to his own beat,
doesn't have a strong presence,

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:42.780
and has nothing in particular going for him.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:47.820
But while he seems ordinary, every now and then
he has these unexpectedly zany ideas

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:50.730
and gets things done when it really matters.

00:12:50.730 --> 00:12:52.700
He is a man of surprising charm.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:53.740
Hmm.

00:12:56.370 --> 00:12:59.960
I see you're not angered
by what I have with Sou-san.

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:02.960
Even if you were to have a boyfriend,

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:06.490
it wouldn't change the fact that you're my fiancée.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:09.350
Now, where would you like to go?

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.740
Anywhere is fine.

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:14.890
Since we're out anyway,
let's go somewhere you've never been before.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:17.800
Somewhere I've never been before...

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:23.650
I had no idea you had any interest in this stuff.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:26.480
"This stuff"? You wound me.

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:30.870
This is an amusement park run by a subsidiary of my company, the Reito Group.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:33.870
So this is what they call a gaming center.

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:38.800
Have you decided?

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:40.740
I'm not sure which one is best for me.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:43.240
Yes!

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:45.480
Hmm, let's see...

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:48.360
Somewhere in this range might be good.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:50.050
That might be too light.

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:52.080
You should take this one.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:54.430
It seems a bit heavy.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.940
I thought so. Might be better to stick with these.

00:13:57.320 --> 00:14:00.960
A novice might not know this,
but with bowling balls,

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:02.940
it's best to choose one
that's a bit on the heavy side.

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:06.900
Thank you very much for that condescending little speech.

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:09.660
You're welcome.

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:25.320
Oh...

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:28.880
No worries, Senpai. That's about how it goes for everyone at first.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.120
You had good form, though.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:40.640
Maybe it's the ball after all.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:42.960
No, her fingers must have slipped.

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:46.750
Senpai, the game's not over yet.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:47.740
This is only the beginning.

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:50.300
I'm starting to get a bit fired up.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:51.950
Your turn is next, right, Sou-san?

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:55.200
As my boyfriend, will you show me
how awesome you can be?

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.470
What? O-Oh!

00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:58.660
Leave it to me!

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:01.640
Do your best.

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:02.420
Will do.

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:24.800
I lowered my center of gravity,
just like you taught me.

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:26.920
You really are a quick study.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.660
I want to see you get involved with my company's operations just as quickly.

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:32.990
Both my father and I think it would be best for us to get married as soon as possible.

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:36.380
Yes, I heard about that from my father.

00:15:36.380 --> 00:15:39.610
Let's form a conglomerate that'll be a global driving force someday.

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:41.510
Yes, let's.

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:45.000
That was no good.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:48.710
You said you hadn't played in a while,
but you put up a good fight too.

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:49.720
No...

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:53.270
You did impressively well for
your first time, Nagisa-senpai.

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:56.230
Um, Reito-san...

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:00.230
How about we play one more game?

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:04.170
I lost.

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:05.630
Good work out there.

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:08.010
I think you put up a perfectly brave fight.

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:09.500
Do you suppose so?

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.920
Well, I'm in the Astronomy Club.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.100
It's not like I'm some kind of jock.

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.200
Sou-san...

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:21.160
How did you meet that guy—I mean, that person?

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:23.230
It was through a matchmaking meeting.

00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:26.210
He's an important business partner of my father's, you see.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:29.180
This is, in part, a contract.

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:30.170
A contract?

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:33.340
He's actually quite the elegant gentleman, isn't he?

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:36.680
And at least now I know he's no slouch when it comes to bowling, either.

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:40.240
My future's already been decided, so...

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:45.980
Well, then, shall we go home?

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:48.600
Reito-san, we came all the way here,

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:50.730
so keep me company for a little bit longer.

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:03.290
Wow, losing to a member of the Astronomy Club?

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:05.420
You must be pretty out of shape.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:08.280
I can't say that winning against a guy who works a desk job says much.

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:23.210
Here.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:29.900
Yes!

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:33.490
Take that! And that! And that!

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.420
Looks like I win this time.

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:38.570
Damn it...

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:40.500
You got me.

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:42.480
Oh? Where's Nagisa-san?

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:43.040
What?

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:46.270
Oh, shoot, and here I was
trying to show off for her.

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:47.130
Ooh!

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:47.870
What's going on?

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:55.130
Oh, there she is.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:05.180
Hey, you two aren't really a couple or anything, are you?

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:08.060
You had that figured out, huh?

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:11.610
It'd be stranger for me <i>not</i> to notice after all that.

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:15.770
I suspect she's not too enthusiastic about marrying me.

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:18.700
Playing at being a couple with you
is her way of expressing that, right?

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:21.390
If you think so, then why...

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:24.410
We're the same. Birds in a cage.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:28.170
It's not as if rebelling will give us
the freedom to choose our futures.

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.840
Nagisa-san should know that better than anyone.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:35.840
And knowing all that, you won't escape from your cage either?

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:39.470
No. I live for my father and the company.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.590
You're good with that?

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:43.510
It's not about good or bad.

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:46.440
When you grow up, you'll understand too.

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:49.150
I... suppose...

00:18:52.050 --> 00:18:53.610
No way!
Whoa!

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:55.610
What the?!

00:18:57.220 --> 00:18:58.030
So cute!

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:01.450
Wow, I didn't know she could smile like that.

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:04.790
If anything, that's the Nagisa-senpai I see every day.

00:19:05.150 --> 00:19:06.100
What?

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:10.000
Do you suppose she'll smile like that
for you inside the cage?

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:11.250
What?

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:13.920
H-Hey...

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:17.360
Senpai, I need to talk to you for a second.

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:18.640
Sou-san?

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:21.030
What? But I'm not done yet.

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:27.760
I'm sorry for dragging you out here.

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:30.640
Leaving Reito-san behind, no less.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:34.480
Sorry for that too. I kind of wanted to talk to you in private.

00:19:34.890 --> 00:19:35.700
I see.

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:38.840
Are you okay with this, Senpai?

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.160
With this marriage...

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:42.670
Or well, engagement... Or well...

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:45.200
I'm used to it now.

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:48.110
I was born into this environment.

00:19:48.110 --> 00:19:49.690
So there's nothing I can do.

00:19:49.690 --> 00:19:51.230
It can't be changed.

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:55.240
When I see that look of resignation on your face...

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:56.570
I kind of hate it.

00:19:57.270 --> 00:19:59.880
Sorry. This isn't about me.

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:04.970
Ever since I was little, I've been encouraged to grow up as quickly as possible.

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:08.110
In point of fact, I was surrounded by grown ups,

00:20:08.110 --> 00:20:11.750
and among them were those who tried to curry favor with me as well.

00:20:13.280 --> 00:20:16.920
No one had any interest in who I really was,

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:19.780
and along the way, I became unable to let my guard down with people.

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:23.480
Let's go home already.

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:25.030
That's not true.

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:28.470
I'm not like those people.

00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:29.830
And neither is the rest of the club.

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:34.000
I don't really understand the environment you grew up in,

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.630
but to let others decide things for you

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:38.480
and say that there's nothing
you can do about it...

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:40.010
That's not like you.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:44.870
Please be your usual high-han—
freewheeling self.

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:47.930
Even if you run into trouble,
I'm sure we can help you.

00:20:49.170 --> 00:20:50.120
At least, I think so.

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:57.690
Wha...

00:20:58.170 --> 00:20:59.880
N-Never mind me!

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.070
How about you worry about your own future?!

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:03.310
Senpai...

00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:04.380
Wh-What?

00:21:04.850 --> 00:21:05.980
That's adorable.

00:21:05.980 --> 00:21:07.760
I-I should hit you for that!

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:09.760
Are you done with your little private chat?

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:11.400
Reito-san...

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:13.180
The sun's setting.

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:15.210
I'll drive you both home.

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:20.800
Man, I'm tired.

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:23.260
What happened to wear you out like that?

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:25.090
It's a long story.

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:26.830
Here you are.

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:27.720
Thanks.

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:31.070
Oh, that's right. Airi-chan had the idea

00:21:31.070 --> 00:21:34.430
that we should do a trial run
making the sweets here tomorrow.

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:35.290
Huh...

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:37.880
So, make sure you stay
at home tomorrow, okay?

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:38.680
What?

00:21:38.680 --> 00:21:40.440
Don't "what" me.

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:44.740
Did something good happen?

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:50.520
I'm starting to feel like the future...

00:21:50.520 --> 00:21:51.990
might not be set in stone after all.

00:23:25.450 --> 00:23:26.340
It was good for photosynthesis as well.

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:27.910
Call it an extracurricular activity.

00:23:27.910 --> 00:23:29.080
Treasure!

00:23:29.080 --> 00:23:29.990
A certain person's face in profile...

00:23:29.990 --> 00:23:31.480
Why did you put those two together?

00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:32.690
Please call me Yui.

00:23:32.690 --> 00:23:34.740
It's light that's reached the end of a great journey.

00:23:35.200 --> 00:23:40.020
Episode seven: "Waiting 2.39 Million Light-years."
